//! What the shared tactics know about particular cards beyond their printed
//! stats: battles they cannot lose, what becomes of a monster that attacks
//! them, effects that cannot reach them, what their owner gets back when
//! they are destroyed.  Every deck plays around them by default; a deck that
//! wants the exception still decides it in its own `Strategy` hooks.
//!
//! The facts come from two places.  `pool.rs` is generated by `policy-bench
//! knowledge`: it stages every monster of the card pool on a plain board,
//! has it attacked, aimed at and attacking, and writes down what the engine
//! did.  The entries in [`facts`] are written by hand, for what a staged
//! board does not show: effects that depend on a coin toss, on the hand or
//! on another card.
//!
//! Facts are looked up by the code the viewer sees (`Ctx::facts`).  The
//! opponent's face-down cards have no code (the seat redacts them before the
//! policy looks), so nothing about a hidden card leaks: it stays an unknown
//! monster until it is flipped or revealed.

mod pool;

